{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-pillow-2026-112392",
  "summary": "Pillow: NULL dereference in ImagingExpand via rank filters on zero-size images",
  "details": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 13.0.0, Pillow's rank-based filters can dereference invalid image storage for a zero-size image. ImagingExpand() allocates a non-empty output and then faults while replicating edges by reading the first pixel from empty input storage; ImagingRankFilter is never reached. An attacker can supply or cause creation of a zero-size image to an application that applies a rank, median, minimum, or maximum filter. This causes a native process crash. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0.",
